From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MilkFlint <milkflint@localhost>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 22:04:40 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] net/sched: sch_cake: no dither for a host's only bulk flow

cake_get_flow_quantum() shares the quantum between a host's bulk flows
with quantum_div[], and dithers with get_random_u16() for the rounding.
For a host with one bulk flow (the usual case, and every sparse flow)
quantum_div[1] stands for 65536, which doesn't fit in a u16, and the
exact answer is the quantum itself: return it without the random number.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 net/sched/sch_cake.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/net/sched/sch_cake.c b/net/sched/sch_cake.c
index 5ee4558..25c70e5 100644
--- a/net/sched/sch_cake.c
+++ b/net/sched/sch_cake.c
@@ -691,6 +691,12 @@ static u16 cake_get_flow_quantum(struct cake_tin_data *q,
 		host_load = max(host_load,
 				q->hosts[flow->dsthost].dsthost_bulk_flow_count);
 
+	/* quantum_div[1] stands for 65536, which doesn't fit in a u16: a host
+	 * with one bulk flow gives it the whole quantum, no dither needed.
+	 */
+	if (host_load == 1)
+		return q->flow_quantum;
+
 	/* The get_random_u16() is a way to apply dithering to avoid
 	 * accumulating roundoff errors
 	 */
